 Please see our [Development guide](docs/development.md) for how to get Fizzy set up for local development.
 
 
+## Deploying on one server
+
+The included [Kamal](https://kamal-deploy.org/) configuration runs Fizzy, SQLite,
+uploads, and background jobs in one container. It requires a Linux server reachable
+by SSH with Docker (or an account that can install Docker), a DNS record pointed at
+that server, an SMTP server, and an image registry such as Docker Hub. Kamal Proxy
+obtains and renews the TLS certificate.
+
+1. In `config/deploy.yml`, replace `YOUR_SERVER_IP`, `YOUR_REGISTRY_USERNAME`,
+   `fizzy.example.com`, and the example mail settings. The value of `proxy.host` and
+   `APP_HOST` must be the same public hostname.
+2. Copy `.kamal/secrets.local.example` to `.kamal/secrets.local`, fill in the registry
+   and SMTP credentials, and generate `SECRET_KEY_BASE` with `bin/rails secret`.
+3. Ensure ports 80 and 443 are open and the hostname's DNS record points to the box,
+   then run `bin/kamal setup`.
+
+Fizzy will be available at `https://your-host`. Its SQLite databases and uploaded
+files are stored in the `fizzy_storage` Docker volume, which is retained when the
+application container is replaced on later `bin/kamal deploy` runs. Back up this
+volume as part of normal server maintenance.
+
 ## Contributing
 
 We welcome contributions! Please read our [style guide](STYLE.md) before submitting code.
diff --git a/config/deploy.yml b/config/deploy.yml
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..5d1130f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/config/deploy.yml
@@ -0,0 +1,45 @@
+# One-box Fizzy deployment. Replace the four YOUR_* / example values below.
+service: fizzy
+image: YOUR_REGISTRY_USERNAME/fizzy
+
+servers:
+  web:
+    - YOUR_SERVER_IP
+
+proxy:
+  ssl: true
+  host: fizzy.example.com
+
+registry:
+  username: YOUR_REGISTRY_USERNAME
+  password:
+    - KAMAL_REGISTRY_PASSWORD
+
+# SQLite databases, Active Storage uploads, Solid Cache, Solid Cable, and
+# Solid Queue all live here. Docker keeps this named volume between deploys.
+volumes:
+  - fizzy_storage:/rails/storage
+
+env:
+  clear:
+    APP_HOST: fizzy.example.com
+    MAILER_FROM_ADDRESS: "Fizzy <fizzy@example.com>"
+    SMTP_ADDRESS: smtp.example.com
+    SMTP_PORT: 587
+    SMTP_DOMAIN: example.com
+    SMTP_AUTHENTICATION: plain
+    SMTP_ENABLE_STARTTLS_AUTO: true
+    # Fizzy's Puma process runs Solid Queue. Do not add a separate jobs role
+    # for this one-container deployment.
+    SOLID_QUEUE_IN_PUMA: true
+  secret:
+    - SECRET_KEY_BASE
+    - SMTP_USERNAME
+    - SMTP_PASSWORD
+
+builder:
+  arch: amd64
+
+aliases:
+  console: app exec --interactive --reuse "bin/rails console"
+  shell: app exec --interactive --reuse "bash"
